        "call-integration-notification-active-speaker-he.png",
        "call-integration-notification-incoming-he.png",
        "call-integration-notification-outgoing-he.png"
      ],
      "description": "At 320dp width and font scale 1.3, Android 13 CallStyle abbreviates long contact names in its header. The active-call header shows only ellipsis because the app name and chronometer consume the header width. Incoming and outgoing calls show the first Hebrew name prefix. Native action text also ellipsizes, while handset, speaker, answer and end icons remain clear. Full accessible descriptions and dispatch are asserted by the native suite, but visual caller identification remains inadequate for the user request.",
      "decision": "Repeat the caller first in the notification body so a meaningful name remains visible. Requires a product fix and fresh native captures before PASS."
    },
    {
      "severity": "minor",
      "files": [
        "call-emerald-dark-normal-largefont.png",
        "call-emerald-dark-normal-longname-he.png",
        "call-emerald-light-normal-largefont.png"
      ],
      "description": "At font1.3 Hebrew New call label ellipsizes in normal three-column control grid. Target and icon remain fully visible. Full accessibility text is asserted in instrumentation per parent context; pixels alone cannot prove it."
    },
    {
      "severity": "expected",
      "description": "Intentionally long names ellipsize; their phone number remains fully readable. No control overlap or vertical clipping observed."
    }
  ],
